  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Galaxy_at_War\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War\">Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War</a></i> </p><p>Used by soldiers for thousands of years, the Entrenching Tool is a durable, multipurpose tool that also can be an effective melee weapon. The Entrenching Tool can be configured as a short shovel, a pickaxe, or even a makeshift hammer. </p><p>The Entrenching Tool is designed to be durable enough for combat, but it is not as balanced as a regular Weapon. The wielder takes a -2 penalty to attack rolls (<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Improvised_Weapons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Improvised Weapons\">Improvised Weapons</a> normally impose a -5 penalty to attack rolls) and can choose to deal either Piercing or Slashing damage. </p>",
